<!-- THE LAUNCHER ICON (the manifest's android:icon; the launcher and the
     recents card). Its glyph is Breeze's music-note-16th, the flagged
     quaver the BPM button wears (assets/icons/breeze/music-note-16th.svg,
     the 22 px action icon, transcribed for the roster as
     Icon::MusicNote16th), with its head and flag FILLED, painted as the
     Linux one paints its note, white at .75 opacity, and centred on that
     one's sheet grey. The Linux one is Breeze's audio-x-generic (the
     packaging/warptempo_gui.desktop's Icon=, vendored verbatim as
     assets/icons/breeze/audio-x-generic.svg, never transcribed) (architect
     2026-09-30, his pick between two mock-ups: "Music note 16th ...
     definitely use the white color, the filled-in note head, the same style
     as the original icon"). Its two earlier renderings that night: the note
     of audio-x-generic alone, centred on the same grey (c8ae868e), stood an
     hour and gave way at his look to the notes on a staff of Breeze's
     minuet-scales in their own dark ink (fd1160df), which stood an hour in
     turn; the whole audio-x-generic file rendered at fit stood one evening,
     2026-09-29. An ADAPTIVE icon, the whole of it: minSdk is 30, so no
     legacy ic_launcher.png set exists beside it.

     Two layers per density under res/mipmap-<density>/:
       ic_launcher_background.png  solid opaque #aaaaaa, the sheet's own fill
                                   in audio-x-generic (fill="#aaa"): the
                                   platter IS the sheet, its edges gone;
       ic_launcher_foreground.png  the filled quaver, RGBA, #ffffff at alpha
                                   .75 (audio-x-generic's note: its group's
                                   fill #fff, its path's opacity .75), on a
                                   transparent surround.

     THE 44-OF-72 RULE. Every mask (circle, squircle, rounded square: the
     launcher's choice) is drawn within the central 72 dp viewport of the
     108 dp canvas; the glyph's bounding box is 44 dp on its longer side
     there, the ordinary launcher-glyph proportion, and centred on the
     canvas. The box, measured by rendering the filled path alone and
     trimming it, is x 6..16, y 3..19 in the file's 22-unit frame (the
     vendored path carries no transform): 10 by 16 units, so the height is
     the longer side, H = 44 dp, and the width follows the aspect,
     W = H·10/16 rounded to a whole pixel by nearbyint (a tie to even).

     THE DERIVED SVG. The recipe's input is android/app/ic_launcher_foreground.svg,
     beside the manifest and outside res/ (aapt2 compiles res/ whole and
     refuses an unknown file there): one path whose d is the vendored
     music-note-16th.svg's d TRUNCATED before its second subpath, the outer
     contour byte for byte through its own closing Z (a verbatim prefix of
     the file's d, so a diff between the two is a transcription bug). The
     dropped second and third subpaths (from "m 1,1.0957031" and from
     "M 9,15") are the two that cut the flag and the head hollow in Breeze's
     outline drawing; without them both are solid. Fill #fff at opacity .75,
     no transform, in a viewBox that is the glyph's box, so the file renders
     the glyph edge to edge.

     A ONE-SHOT, NOT A BUILD STEP: the PNGs are rendered once on the laptop and
     committed; a retouch is a re-run of this recipe, never a build step
     (build_apk.sh only compiles res/). The recipe, from the repo root
     (rsvg-convert 2.62, ImageMagick 7), for each density n at factor f
     (mdpi 1, hdpi 1.5, xhdpi 2, xxhdpi 3, xxxhdpi 4) with C = 108·f,
     H = 44·f, W = nearbyint(H·10/16), and the page offsets
     L = (C − W) / 2 (a half pixel where C − W is odd) and T = (C − H) / 2
     = 32·f:

       mdpi     C=108 H=44  W=28  L=40    T=32
       hdpi     C=162 H=66  W=41  L=60.5  T=48
       xhdpi    C=216 H=88  W=55  L=80.5  T=64
       xxhdpi   C=324 H=132 W=82  L=121   T=96
       xxxhdpi  C=432 H=176 W=110 L=161   T=128

       rsvg-convert -w W -h H \
           - -page-width C - -page-height C - -left L - -top T \
           android/app/ic_launcher_foreground.svg -o fg.png
       magick fg.png -strip -define png:compression-level=9 \
           -define png:compression-filter=5 \
           PNG32:android/app/res/mipmap-n/ic_launcher_foreground.png
       magick -size CxC xc:'#aaaaaa' -strip \
           PNG8:android/app/res/mipmap-n/ic_launcher_background.png

     (The long options are spelt "- -" above only because an XML comment may
     not hold two adjacent hyphens: type them as the usual double hyphen.)
     The foreground stays RGBA: a palette encoding of it is not lossless (its
     antialiased alpha edges), while the one-colour background is. -->
<adaptive-icon xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <background android:drawable="@mipmap/ic_launcher_background"/>
    <foreground android:drawable="@mipmap/ic_launcher_foreground"/>
</adaptive-icon>
